<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Why Eritrea matters as fighting returns to Ethiopia's Tigray</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d662a6b6810ec070846c4c72a4795d9bf11f28cb55f3831aa2013d3a6c0bf011</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-eritrea-matters-as-fighting-returns-to-ethiopia-s-tigray/a-79426582--8b6ce123ee44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-eritrea-matters-as-fighting-returns-to-ethiopia-s-tigray/a-79426582?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has removed key sanctions on Eritrea as Houthi attacks disrupt Red Sea shipping and fighting escalates in Ethiopia's Tigray region. Analysts say Eritrea's strategic value is growing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Internet disrupted in Tigray amid conflict escalation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3626d7f88192f3abb79ab8cfd3561ea982f0b73cf71ecd078363f11c08c0d1</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T07:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-internet-disrupted-in-tigray-amid-conflict-escalation/a-79424191--15879d4d7c53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-internet-disrupted-in-tigray-amid-conflict-escalation/a-79424191?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A web monitor reported an internet disruption in northern Ethiopia amid renewed fighting between the Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) and the federal government.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How renewed fighting in Tigray could spread across the Horn of Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c339f08b114fe11be73f2e884c88ab38728ac66d47497cff794a4ceb77622430</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333--a598375bf2c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-renewed-fighting-in-tigray-could-spread-across-the-horn-of-africa/a-79410333?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fresh hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region come after months of growing animosity between rebel forces and the federal government. Horn of Africa expert Martin Plaut warns of possible regional spillover.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia's military says it killed hundreds of TPLF rebels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d91e2399e3138353981b2e5b3f7e91b49f74c09390af96948198199e5c12a0e4</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173--d10c751c44c1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ethiopia-s-military-says-it-killed-hundreds-of-tplf-rebels/a-79419173?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The TPLF fought against against the Ethiopian military from 2020 to 2022 in a conflict that saw hundreds of thousands of civilians killed. A resumption of fighting has sparked fears of another brutal war.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria, US agree to boost mining investment on sidelines of UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a07013b3d47c63946df9766ba94a6f38a7a334fcc5988a19817e13e95655eea0</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T15:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444--0b49b11ac5c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-us-agree-to-boost-mining-investment-on-sidelines-of-un-general-assembly/a-79417444?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On the sidelines of the UN General Assembly, Nigeria and the US inked a new mining deal. Nigeria is home to deposits of lithium, gold, tin, gemstones, iron ore and phosphate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Morocco: Center-right PAM leads in parliamentary election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6eb1ec737f497db36708baaa81e45a136d5b995f97e998cd3acd091c74badd06</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T08:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/morocco-center-right-pam-leads-in-parliamentary-election/a-79407710--cbd3d630bc57.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/morocco-center-right-pam-leads-in-parliamentary-election/a-79407710?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">PAM is part of Morocco's outgoing ruling coalition and was founded by an adviser to the king. The moderate Islamist Justice and Development Party surged amid increasing voter apathy.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c606f30ea20ba6b5d5d3b6b3012292e7203358d542c9f44421ea4fa91a5f952</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Decolonizing perceptions about Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca58f5f00507f38717695eb7890eddf6009be86ec5240c5f0a774a3380c7a0cf</id><updated>2026-09-26T05:10:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178--8deea6e78a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a UN resolution alters the standard global map to reflect the continent more accurately, initiatives to decolonize African schools and a campaign to present positive developments are changing the way Africa is seen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
